atterns for  different occasions and different  holidays we bought this neutral wrapping  paper for four dollars and i have since  wrapped several gifts with it but by  contrast i could have purchased this  3.50 bag for a one-time use if you want  to add a personal touch you can use  ribbon yarn a note card or a bow and  chances are you have an empty amazon box  lying around the house that's completely  free so make use of those empty boxes  and save some cash the next time you  need to give a gift number three while  we're on the topic of gifts know your  loved one's love language i really want  to take the time to address gifts  because i feel like when we talk about  saving money we often talk about the  things that you cut back on but when it  comes to physical gifts i feel like  they're important for some people but  not for everybody and i don't think that  you always have to spend money to make  someone feel loved actually you may even  spend hundreds of dollars looking for  the perfect gift for someone only to  find that it didn't have the effect that  you had hoped for a few years ago i read  the life-changing book the five  languages of love and this book taught  me the importance of knowing my love  language how to recognize my love  language and how to spot it in someone  else so why am i even mentioning this  and why is this important i'll give you  an example for the longest time my  husband would make me things he'd spend  hours and hours making me things he's  made me decorative boxes jewelry  furniture and even though i could  recognize those things as sweet and i  saw that his intentions were good i  recognized when i read this book that i  feel most loved when people spend time  with me you see my love language is  quality time i couldn't care less if i  never got a gift in my entire life i  want the thing that cannot be wrapped in  a box time if you've ever gone out and  spent so much time looking for the  perfect gift for someone the perfect  wrapping paper making the bow pristine  and then had the sad realization that it  was a total flop consider their love  language for example if your mom's love  language is acts of service then deep  cleaning her kitchen is going to mean so  much more than a bouquet of roses for  her birthday if your girlfriend lights  up when you spend quality time together  then a walk in the park is going to mean  so much more than a beautiful pair of  earrings or if your friend lights up  when hearing words of affirmation then a  handwritten letter will mean the world  and even if your loved one does feel  most loved when receiving gifts it could  just mean that maybe it would be extra  special if you didn't go the easy route  and buy a gift but instead make them  something that shows that you put forth  some effort so the next time that you  need to give a gift consider that  person's love language and gift them in  their love language it may save you  money and be so much cheaper for you but  i assure you that they're bound to have  a much more positive reaction because  you're speaking to them in the way that  they express love number four if you're  someone that tends to have leftovers  when you go out to eat check out what  the kids meal portions are like at  certain restaurants i remember a few  months back we went to an olive garden  and our daughter got a large plate of  pasta and chicken tenders for a fraction  of the cost of a regular dish but the  portion was definitely enough to where i  thought i would be satiated i mean it  wasn't to where i felt like i'd be full  but definitely enough to satisfy and  some mexican restaurants that we've been  to have served some pretty decent  portions that have left me thinking i  wish i had ordered her meal this is a  kid's meal from a thai restaurant that  we went to and it was significantly  cheaper than our adults meals can i just  say that it looks pretty darn appetizing  just be cautious with this though  because some restaurants may not want  adults to order from the kids meal  because of course they don't make as  much money with this and they don't want  everybody ordering from the kid's meal  so don't tell him yes he sent you  number five this one is totally random  but it's my recent game changer if you  do a lot of cooking and baking at home  then consider swapping out your  disposable oil spray bottle for a  reusable bottle instead and really in  general reusable items save you so much  more money in the long run i actually  have two videos on lots of reusable  items that you can swap out for some big  money savings but this one's just my  most recent swap i was buying these  little disposable bottles at our grocery  store for around three dollars each when  i could have just been buying a big tub  of oil and refilling the bottle when it  runs out i think that our big jug of  olive oil was like 15 or something like  that so i'm really excited that now we  don't ever have to buy the disposables  again and that we can just use this much  cheaper alternative number six while  we're on the topic of food this one is  not one that i currently do but it's one  that i used to do when i worked as a  nurse on night shift and we used to do  this actually weekly and that is to have  potlucks for lunch if you work in an  office area or a place that has a  designated break room or work room a  potluck can be a great way to save some  extra cash because even though you do  spend some money on sharing some food  you're bound to have a variety of  choices and at least for us we always  had enough for our 12-hour shifts and  some take-home food but it really became  a fun way to save money and because we  did it so frequently we had a sign-up  sheet that had the dates that we would  be doing the potluck and who would be  bringing what and so if your job doesn't  have something like this maybe you can  arrange it and it could be a really fun  way to get to know your co-workers and  save some money i