ey would normally because  they have lots of promotions all the  time where they give you extra points  for certain purchases and they're all  constantly changing and then the other  reason is that it gives you more money  for popular brands and processed foods  rather than like fresh fruits and  veggies which is most of what i buy so i  don't consider it to be like a  significant money maker for me but hey i  mean it's free money right because i  personally do have fetch and i've used  it for several months i have my referral  link down below but you do not have to  use my link or even use a link at all  you can go directly to the app if you  feel more comfortable with that number  12 i kind of hinted at the beginning of  this video it should come as no surprise  that my single most favorite way to save  money on the daily is to swap out  disposable items for reusable ones  instead because every time you toss that  old dish sponge or napkin in the trash  you're literally tossing your  hard-earned cash in the trash sometimes  reusable items do require a little extra  work for example cloth diapering but  you'd be surprised how much these  reusable alternatives can save you  clutter time and space because you don't  have to buy packs and cases of things so  the amount that you would spend in the  long run can really add up so look  around your home and find the items that  you're disposing of most and try finding  a reusable option for those there are  tons of reusable alternatives out there  and you don't have to go to extremes and  use reusable toilet paper but even just  cutting down on some of the things that  you're disposing of the most can really  go a long way towards cutting down on  your expenses that's it for today's  video those are my 12 simple small and  easy ways to help you save money so that  you can spend it on the things that  matter most to you i thank you so much  for watching and if you like this video  please give it a thumbs up and subscribe  